<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis V, Landgrave of Hesse-Darmstadt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1577–1626</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis V was landgrave of Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> from 1596 to 1626. A Lutheran loyal to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> emperors, he founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-giessen">University of Giessen</a> in 1607 and gained much of the disputed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marburg">Marburg</a> inheritance during <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. In 1622 he granted Homburg to his brother Frederick, founding the line of Hesse-Homburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-v-landgrave-of-hesse-darmstadt.jpg" alt="Louis V, Landgrave of Hesse-Darmstadt" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Kilian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:L_kilian_landgraf_ludwig_1615.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
